From 20cf85139a73fb310e900ea713b9925c548dc66a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Georg Richter <georg@mariadb.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:03:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Branch 3.4 after 3.4.11: Merge branch '3.3' into 3.4
 (CONC-861, CONC-i860, CONC-i864, CONC-863)

The change that merge commit 486a0223ee8727990cf74bc2631ac2cd2c673fc3 of the 3.4 branch of
https://github.com/mariadb-corporation/mariadb-connector-c brought,
taken as it landed on that branch (the diff against its first parent).
The commits it merges, with their own messages:

----- 1d49ef62c97021b7f8c13b59221c5a2a0c97c155
Author: Georg Richter <georg@mariadb.com>
Date:   Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:08:40 +0200

CONC-861: Bounds checks for length-encoded integers and binary rows

Add net_field_length_safe()/net_field_length_ll_safe(), which take an end
pointer, reject 0xFF, truncated prefixes and 32-bit overflow, and
optionally reject the NULL marker (MARIADB_LENENC_FORBID_NULL).

Export mariadb_net_field_length() (version node libmariadb_3_3_22).

Use the checked decoders in cli_report_progress(),
mthd_my_read_query_result(), mthd_my_read_one_row(),
mysql_list_processes(), mthd_stmt_read_all_rows(),
mthd_stmt_flush_unbuffered() and mthd_stmt_fetch_to_bind().

mthd_stmt_fetch_to_bind() now owns the column boundary: it validates the
length prefix and the lengths of temporal types, and resyncs the row
pointer after callbacks and conversion functions.

Behavior changes: malformed text rows report CR_MALFORMED_PACKET instead
of CR_UNKNOWN_ERROR; EOF packets shorter than 5 bytes are rejected.

Assisted by Claude

